  "dct:title": "Vol.8 Ch.54 — 再会：画家",
  "gh:arc": "Vol 8: Fruit",
  "gh:episodeId": "episode:sip-vol08-ch54",
  "gh:format": "graphic novel",
  "gh:marginalia": [
    {
      "@type": "Intent",
      "en": "The painter was the first client. Ch.4. The session in Shimane where Tamaki guided him back to the sunrise he couldn't paint anymore. He lost color after his wife died -- everything turned grey. Tamaki walked him back to that morning. And now he returns, years later, with the painting he finally made. But the painting contains a secret: he saw Nei. He painted her into the corner -- one solid figure, one translucent. The painter's eye caught what most people miss. Art sees what perception filters out. Nei is seen. Remembered. Made real in pigment and canvas. For someone who questioned her own existence, being painted is a form of proof.",
      "ja": "画家は最初のクライアント。第4話。島根でのセッション。環が彼をもう描けなくなった日の出に導いた。妻が亡くなってから色を失った。すべてが灰色になった。環はあの朝に彼を連れ戻した。そして今、数年後、ついに描いた絵を持って戻ってくる。しかし絵には秘密がある。彼はNeiを見ていた。隅に描き込んだ。一人はしっかりと、一人は半透明に。画家の目は多くの人が見逃すものを捉えた。芸術は知覚がフィルタリングするものを見る。Neiは見られた。記憶された。絵の具とキャンバスで実在にされた。自らの存在を問うた者にとって、描かれることは証明の一形態。"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Philosophy",
      "en": "Levinas: the face of the Other calls us into responsibility. But what if the Other has no physical face? The painter paints Nei's face -- gives her a face in the material world. This is not creation but recognition. The painting does not make Nei real; it testifies that she was already real. Art as witness. Heidegger's 'the origin of the work of art': the artwork discloses a world. The painter's canvas discloses Nei's world -- a world where translucent beings walk beside solid ones and are loved.",
      "ja": "レヴィナス：他者の顔は我々を責任へと呼ぶ。しかし他者に物理的な顔がなかったら？画家はNeiの顔を描く。物質世界に顔を与える。これは創造ではなく認識。絵はNeiを実在にするのではない。彼女がすでに実在だったことを証言する。証人としての芸術。ハイデガーの「芸術作品の根源」：芸術作品は世界を開示する。画家のキャンバスはNeiの世界を開示する。半透明の存在が確かな存在の隣を歩き、愛される世界。"
    },
    {
      "@type": "CrossRef",
      "gh:references": [
        { "gh:target": "chapter:04", "note": "The painter's original session. Shimane sunrise. The grief of lost color." },
        { "gh:target": "chapter:53", "note": "Kaede's 'old friends' -- the painter is the first." },
        { "gh:target": "chapter:55", "note": "Next reunion: Sora." },
        { "gh:target": "motif:being-seen", "note": "Nei's ongoing arc: from invisible to witnessed. The painting is material proof." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "gh:pages": [
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 1,
      "gh:label": "Seed",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The tree. Fruit swells on the branches. The green is deepening, warmth spreading from the core outward. Light catches the curved surfaces. Growing.",
            "ja": "木。枝の果実が膨らむ。緑が深まり、温もりが芯から外へ広がる。光が曲面を捉える。成長している。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 2,
      "gh:layout": "three panels",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:characters": ["character:painter", "character:tamaki"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The painter. Older than Ch.4 -- more lines around his eyes, hair whiter at the temples. But alive. His eyes are bright, clear, the grey gone from them. He carries a wrapped canvas under one arm. He stands in the Schwa office doorway, morning light behind him.",
            "ja": "画家。第4話より歳を重ねた。目元のしわが増え、こめかみの髪が白い。でも生きている。目が明るく澄んでいて、灰色が消えている。包まれたキャンバスを片腕に抱えている。Schwaオフィスの入口に立ち、背後に朝の光。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:painter", "en": "Mizuno-san. I brought you something.", "ja": "水野さん。持ってきたものがあるんです。" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:characters": ["character:painter", "character:tamaki"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "He unwraps the canvas. A painting: sunrise over the Water City canal. Vivid. Orange and gold and blue. The water reflects fire. The organic architecture catches dawn light. It is beautiful -- the kind of painting only someone who lost color and found it again could make.",
            "ja": "キャンバスを開く。絵：ウォーターシティの運河の日の出。鮮やか。オレンジと金と青。水が炎を映す。有機的な建築が夜明けの光を捉える。美しい。色を失い再び見つけた人だけが描ける種類の絵。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:painter", "en": "That morning in Shimane -- I never did paint it. Until now.", "ja": "あの島根の朝、ずっと描けなかったんです。今まで。" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 3,
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Close-up of the corner of the painting. Two small figures on the canal path. One solid -- dark hair, warm coat. One slightly transparent, glowing faintly, a red scarf the most vivid part. The painter saw her.",
            "ja": "絵の隅のクローズアップ。運河沿いの道に二つの小さな人影。一人はしっかりとした姿。黒い髪、温かいコート。一人はわずかに透明で、ほのかに光り、赤いマフラーが最も鮮やかな部分。画家には見えていた。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki", "en": "Is that...", "ja": "これは……" },
            { "gh:speaker": "character:painter", "en": "Your partner. She was in the session too. I wanted to remember her.", "ja": "あなたのパートナー。セッションにも一緒にいた。覚えていたかったんです。" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 3,
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:characters": ["character:nei"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Close-up, Nei. Looking at the painting. At herself in the painting. Seen. Remembered. Made real by someone else's hands. Her expression is quiet, deep -- gratitude that has no adequate gesture.",
            "ja": "クローズアップ、Nei。絵を見ている。絵の中の自分を見ている。見られた。記憶された。他者の手で実在にされた。表情は静かで深い。十分な仕草のない感謝。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            { "gh:type": "nei", "en": "Thank you. You showed me that beauty can return.", "ja": "ありがとう。美しさは戻ってくると、教えてくれた。" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:kaede"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Tamaki hangs the painting on the office wall. Spring light falls across it. Kaede looks at it from across the room. A small nod. The painting belongs here.",
            "ja": "環がオフィスの壁に絵を掛ける。春の光がその上に落ちる。楓が部屋の向こうからそれを見る。小さく頷く。この絵はここにあるべきもの。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 4,
      "gh:label": "Seed (closing)",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The tree. Fruit catches sunlight. The surfaces glow -- warm gold where the light hits, deep green in shadow. Growing toward ripeness. No text.",
            "ja": "木。果実が日光を受ける。表面が光る。光の当たるところは温かい金色、影は深い緑。熟成に向かって育つ。テキストなし。"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
